description |
  bench/unusual@0.1 -- the unusual-features set. This file carries ONLY the
  `ext bench` capability matrix (the pattern source is subbench.toml's
  [[patterns]] array + patterns/*.rx); every block below is a verbatim copy of
  bench/capability/patterns.rxt's, so an engine fact is declared in one place
  (gen_patterns.py --check), then this set's own callout facts (L5,
  gen_patterns.py UNUSUAL_DELTA): `callouts` for pcrec (link-time binding) and
  Oniguruma (`(?CN)` respelled `(?{N})`), `unusual-co-netstr` for pcrec only,
  `unusual-co-*-nofn` for libpcre2 only; the `vars` + `unusual-va-*` tokens are
  declared for pcrec's native-vars configs only (L7, VARS_NATIVE). The
  `*-assist-v01` configs copy their base's block (b148aw, ASSIST_ARMS); their
  ASSISTED members' `unusual-<member>` grants are read from assists.tsv at run
  time. `unusual-<member>` of a recursion/callout member is declared wherever
  the block already satisfies the member's other requires (FEATURE_MEMBERS).

oracle pcre2
tag set=unusual, version=0.1
ext bench
  roster pcre2-interp pcre2-jit pcrec-auto pcrec-nocaps pcrec-vm pcrec-vm-in re2-default onig-default vectorscan-block-som rust-default pcre2-interp-deep pcre2-jit-deep pcrec-auto-deep pcrec-vm-deep onig-default-deep pcre2-jit-assist-v01 onig-default-assist-v01 re2-default-assist-v01 rust-default-assist-v01 vectorscan-block-som-assist-v01
  capabilities pcre2-interp
    backrefs
    lookaround
    lookbehind-variable
    possessive-quantifier
    atomic-group
    recursion
    conditionals
    k-reset
    control-verbs
    unicode-properties
    named-groups
    free-spacing
    callouts
    span-reporting
    non-utf8-subject
    captures
    true-end-anchor
    unusual-co-luhn-nofn
    unusual-co-isbn-nofn
    unusual-co-member-nofn
    unusual-cscan
